Crystal plate is *heavy*.  It can be a good idea to replace it
with one of the two types of mithril from the mines even though
mithril doesn't have as good an AC rating.  The difference in
the wieght means you can carry a lot of other items without
getting Burdened or worse.

> Here's the first question.  Cleaver, or Frost Brand?

Frosty hands down.  Second/third best weapon in the game
for any alignment, best available to neutrals.  Whether
it is the best or second best for chaotics is a matter
of perspective.

> Second, How do I increase their enchantments?

A medium-common type of scroll.

> Thirdly, this demon is following me around (Yeenoghu or something) is
> there a way to make him tame like a pet, because right now he just gets
> in my way >:P

That only happened because you sacaficed a member of your
own race on the altar and you are chaotic.  if you don't
want this to happen in future games, don't do that again.

Y will stay close to you but not *every* move.  Y will
only follow you up or down stairs if he's adjacent when
you climb/descend.  So the strategy is: get fast, go
down a couple of levels.  Dance on and off of the stairs
until he's two away not one.  Dash up the stairs and
never go down to that level again.  Once you have the
stone from mines end there is no more need to go below
mine town.  Alternate stratgey - barbarian smash.  Very
high risk of dying before Y dies at your current level.

